      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Cape Mendocino Lighthouse Preservation Society, founded in 2008, runs a museum and visitor center that showcases original lamps, lenses, and historic documents.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        3,
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://museumsdatabase.com/museums/view/3167",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The society also offers guided tours of the lighthouse, teaching visitors about its construction and role in maritime navigation.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://museumsdatabase.com/museums/view/3167",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Whitethorn sits along California’s Lost Coast, a rugged stretch known for its black sand beaches, mountain bike trails, and abundant wildlife.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18,
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.visitlostcoast.com/points-of-interest-ca/",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "About 1.5 miles south of Whitethorn lies Redwoods Monastery, a community of Cistercian nuns that has been active for decades.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
